<div id="features" class="features">
  <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="capture-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="capture-title">Highlight in Safari. Keep the source.</h2>
      <p>On Mac, select text and press <kbd>⌃⇧H</kbd>, or turn on auto-highlight. On iPhone, select text and choose Twine from Safari's page menu. Each highlight keeps its page title and a link back.</p>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li>Saved highlights return when a page's text still matches</li>
        <li>Source links open at the saved passage</li>
        <li>Option-click to remove on Mac, or double-tap on iPhone</li>
        <li>Undo a removal from the page</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="media">
      {% shot "capture", "mac", "The training section of Wikipedia's large language model article in Safari, with the passage about model training costs highlighted in yellow.", "Safari on a public article with one or two saved Twine highlights. No transient messages or recording needed.", false, "macOS · Save a passage in Safari", 1960, 1280 %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature feature-library" aria-labelledby="library-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="library-title">Find the highlight you need.</h2>
      <p>Browse by website and page, search the words you remember, or narrow by date. Explore the included starter library, then add your own highlights. Copy or share them as plain text or Markdown.</p>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li>Organized by website and page</li>
        <li>Search highlight text, page titles and websites</li>
        <li>A shared library on Mac and iPhone through your private iCloud</li>
        <li>Find highlights in Spotlight or open them from Shortcuts</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="media">
      {% shot "library-duo", "duo", "An open Duo with Twine's All Highlights library on the left and the selected Wikipedia training-cost passage, background explanation and actions on the right.", "The open Duo in landscape orientation, with the library and selected highlight details visible side by side.", false, "Duo · Your library and the details, side by side", 2000, 1407 %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="ai-title">Let your AI tools read your highlights.</h2>
      <p>AI Access lets a compatible AI tool search your highlights, read the saved passages and link to their sources. Turn it on to run Twine's read-only MCP server on your Mac.</p>
      <ul class="prompts" role="list" aria-label="Example requests">
        <li>Find my highlights about onboarding and group them by theme.</li>
        <li>Compare what my saved sources say about remote work, with links to each page.</li>
        <li>Use my highlights from the past week to outline a research brief, and list the excerpts you used.</li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li>Off until you turn it on, and reachable only from your Mac</li>
        <li>Protected by an access token you can replace at any time</li>
        <li>Tools can search, read and export your highlights, but never change them</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">Example requests for a connected AI tool, not a built-in Twine chat. Responses depend on your tool and the highlights you've saved.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="media media-settings">
      {% shot "ai-access", "window", "Twine's AI settings on a Mac with AI Access enabled, a local server URL and controls to copy connection settings or regenerate the token; no token value is displayed.", "Twine Settings > AI > AI Access, with the local server enabled and connection controls visible. Keep access tokens concealed; no chat response needed.", false, "macOS · Connect the AI tools you choose", 1040, 1436 %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="context-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="context-title">See how a passage fits.</h2>
      <p>AI context uses Apple Intelligence on your device to explain how a highlight fits into the surrounding text. Read the explanation under <strong>Background</strong> in the highlight's details.</p>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li>Off until you turn it on</li>
        <li>Saved with the highlight and synced to your other devices</li>
        <li>Writing or refreshing an explanation needs Apple Intelligence</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="media">
      {% shot "context", "phone", "An iPhone showing the highlighted Wikipedia training-cost passage, its Background explanation, the Refresh control and the source.", "An iPhone highlight detail with a completed AI context explanation. Use a public passage with enough surrounding text; avoid loading or unavailable states.", false, "iPhone · Read a passage in context", 1206, 2622 %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="privacy-title">Your library stays yours.</h2>
    <div>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li>No Twine account to create</li>
        <li>Highlights live on your devices and sync through your private iCloud. The developer never receives them.</li>
        <li>No analytics, ads or trackers, in the app or on this site.</li>
        <li>AI Access is off until you turn it on. The connection stays on your Mac; a tool you connect handles what it reads under its own privacy policy.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="more"><a class="text-link" href="/privacy">Read the privacy policy</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

